      "text": "To solve the equation \\(7^{x+7} = 8^x\\) and express the solution in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\), we will follow a step-by-step approach.\n\n1. **Rewrite the equation:**\n   \\[\n   7^{x+7} = 8^x\n   \\]\n\n2. **Express both sides with the same base using the properties of exponents:**\n   \\[\n   7^x \\cdot 7^7 = 8^x\n   \\]\n\n3. **Rearrange the equation to isolate terms involving \\(x\\):**\n   \\[\n   7^x \\cdot 7^7 = 8^x\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   7^7 = 8^x / 7^x\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   7^7 = \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)^x\n   \\]\n\n4. **Take the logarithm of both sides to solve for \\(x\\):**\n   Let \\(y = \\log_7 8\\). Then, \\(\\log_7 8 = y\\).\n   \\[\n   7^7 = \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)^x\n   \\]\n   Taking the logarithm base 7 on both sides:\n   \\[\n   \\log_7 (7^7) = \\log_7 \\left(\\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)^x\\right)\n   \\]\n   Using the logarithm power rule \\(\\log_b (a^c) = c \\log_b a\\):\n   \\[\n   7 \\log_7 7 = x \\log_7 \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)\n   \\]\n   Since \\(\\log_7 7 = 1\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   7 = x \\log_7 \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{7}{\\log_7 \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Express \\(\\log_7 \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)\\) in terms of a base \\(b\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\log_7 \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right) = \\log_7 8 - \\log_7 7 = y - 1\n   \\]\n   Therefore:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{7}{y - 1}\n   \\]\n\n6. **We are given the solution in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\):**\n   \\[\n   x = \\log_b 7^7\n   \\]\n   Using the power rule of logarithms \\(\\log_b (a^c) = c \\log_b a\\):\n   \\[\n   x = 7 \\log_b 7\n   \\]\n\n7. **Equate the two expressions for \\(x\\):**\n   \\[\n   7 \\log_b 7 = \\frac{7}{y - 1}\n   \\]\n   Since \\(y = \\log_7 8\\), we need to find \\(y - 1\\):\n   \\[\n   y - 1 = \\log_7 8 - 1 = \\log_7 8 - \\log_7 7 = \\log_7 \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)\n   \\]\n   Therefore:\n   \\[\n   7 \\log_b 7 = \\frac{7}{\\log_7 \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying:\n   \\[\n   \\log_b 7 = \\frac{1}{\\log_7 \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)}\n   \\]\n\n8. **Express \\(\\log_7 \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)\\) in terms of base \\(b\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\log_7 \\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right) = \\log_7 8 - \\log_7 7 = y - 1\n   \\]\n   Therefore:\n   \\[\n   \\log_b 7 = \\frac{1}{y - 1}\n   \\]\n\n9. **Solve for \\(b\\):**\n   Since \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   \\log_b 7^7 = \\log_b (7^7) = 7 \\log_b 7\n   \\]\n   We already know:\n   \\[\n   7 \\log_b 7 = \\frac{7}{y - 1}\n   \\]\n   Therefore:\n   \\[\n   7 \\log_b 7 = \\frac{7}{y - 1}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying:\n   \\[\n   \\log_b 7 = \\frac{1}{y - 1}\n   \\]\n\n10. **Final answer:**\n    \\[\n    b = \\boxed{7}\n    \\]",
