      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the equation \\(7^{x+7} = 8^x\\) and express the solution in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Express both sides with the same base:**\n   Since the bases are different (7 and 8), we need to express both sides with the same base. However, in this case, converting directly to the same base is complex. Instead, we will use logarithms to simplify the equation.\n\n2. **Take the natural logarithm (or any logarithm) of both sides:**\n   Let's take the natural logarithm (ln) of both sides of the equation:\n   \\[\n   \\ln(7^{x+7}) = \\ln(8^x)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Use the logarithm power rule:**\n   The power rule of logarithms states that \\(\\ln(a^b) = b \\ln(a)\\). Applying this rule, we get:\n   \\[\n   (x + 7) \\ln(7) = x \\ln(8)\n   \\]\n\n4. **Distribute and rearrange the equation:**\n   Distribute \\(\\ln(7)\\) on the left side:\n   \\[\n   x \\ln(7) + 7 \\ln(7) = x \\ln(8)\n   \\]\n   Now, isolate the terms involving \\(x\\):\n   \\[\n   x \\ln(7) - x \\ln(8) = -7 \\ln(7)\n   \\]\n\n5. **Factor out \\(x\\):**\n   Factor \\(x\\) on the left side:\n   \\[\n   x (\\ln(7) - \\ln(8)) = -7 \\ln(7)\n   \\]\n\n6. **Solve for \\(x\\):**\n   Divide both sides by \\(\\ln(7) - \\ln(8)\\):\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{-7 \\ln(7)}{\\ln(7) - \\ln(8)}\n   \\]\n\n7. **Express the solution in the desired form:**\n   We are given that the solution is in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\). Recall that \\(\\log_b a = \\frac{\\ln a}{\\ln b}\\). Therefore:\n   \\[\n   x = \\log_b 7^7 = \\frac{\\ln(7^7)}{\\ln(b)}\n   \\]\n   Simplify the numerator:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{7 \\ln(7)}{\\ln(b)}\n   \\]\n\n8. **Equate the two expressions for \\(x\\):**\n   Since both expressions represent \\(x\\), set them equal to each other:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{7 \\ln(7)}{\\ln(b)} = \\frac{-7 \\ln(7)}{\\ln(7) - \\ln(8)}\n   \\]\n\n9. **Solve for \\(\\ln(b)\\):**\n   Cross-multiply to solve for \\(\\ln(b)\\):\n   \\[\n   7 \\ln(7) (\\ln(7) - \\ln(8)) = -7 \\ln(7) \\ln(b)\n   \\]\n   Divide both sides by \\(7 \\ln(7)\\):\n   \\[\n   \\ln(7) - \\ln(8) = -\\ln(b)\n   \\]\n   Simplify:\n   \\[\n   \\ln(7) - \\ln(8) = -\\ln(b)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\ln(7) - \\ln(8) = -\\ln(b)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\ln(b) = \\ln\\left(\\frac{8}{7}\\right)\n   \\]\n\n10. **Determine \\(b\\):**\n    Convert the logarithmic form to its exponential form:\n    \\[\n    b = \\frac{8}{7}\n    \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(b\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{8}{7}}\\).",
