      "text": "Let $y = x + 7$. The equation becomes $7^y = (\\frac{7}{8})^y$. Taking the logarithm power rule on both sides, we get $\\log(7^y) = y \\log(\\frac{7}{8})$. Since $\\log(a^b) = b \\log(a)$, we can rewrite this as $y \\log(7) + y \\log(\\frac{1}{8}) = 0$. Since $\\log(\\frac{1}{8}) = -\\log(8)$, this simplifies to $y \\log(7) - y \\log(8) = 0$. Factoring out $y$, we see that $y(\\log(7) - \\log(8)) = 0$. Since $y$ is not $0$, we have $\\log(7) - \\log(8) = 0$. Thus, $\\log(7) = \\log(8)$, which means $7 = 8$. Solving for $x$, we have $x + 7 = 6$, so $x = -1$. Since the solution of the equation is in the form $x = \\log_b 7^7$, we have $\\boxed{b = \\frac{7^7}{7}}$.",
